From 0d82f77cd11d1d594fd293210a52376d3b52a684 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lorik Dalloshi <lorik@Loriks-MacBook-Pro.local>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 22:45:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(macos): verified writes, window pinning, paste entry
 and diff read-back

- set_value reads the value back and fails when the control ignored the
  write (#83 finding 2). Text fields inside web content are filled with
  real keystrokes so frameworks such as React register the edit; a native
  text field that ignores the AX write is retried with keystrokes.
- type_text resolves focus live instead of from the cached snapshot,
  falls back to the field last clicked when macOS reports no focus for a
  background app, verifies the field changed and returns a WARNING when it
  did not. AX-write typing is confirmed by read-back before reporting
  success. New method: auto | keys | paste (clipboard + Cmd+V, clipboard
  restored).
- get_app_state window_id / window_title pin a window: snapshots, actions
  and read-backs stay on it (#83 finding 1). The header lists the app's
  windows; an action whose read-back lands on another window says so.
- OPEN_COMPUTER_USE_ACTION_RESULT=diff returns only changed tree lines
  when the window is unchanged and few lines moved (#16, #83 finding 6a);
  OPEN_COMPUTER_USE_ACTION_SCREENSHOT=0 skips read-back capture.
- OPEN_COMPUTER_USE_APP_VARIANT=dev builds an optimized app with the Dev
  bundle identity.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
